<title>NETHERLANDS: NKF H1 NET PROFIT UP 6.8 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>NKF H1 NET PROFIT UP 6.8 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>First half 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per shr (guilders)	     3.51 vs   3.11</p>
<p>    Net profit			    21.9  vs  20.5</p>
<p>    Turnover			     618.7  vs 579.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Cable maker NKF Holding NV reiterated its previous</p>
<p>forecast that the 1996 full-year net profit would at least match</p>
<p>the 1995 level. The company said in March it expected stable</p>
<p>earnings in 1996 and profit growth in later years.</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    38.9  vs  35.0</p>
<p>    Interest charges		     6.9  vs   9.0</p>
<p>    Tax				     10.1  vs   5.5</p>
<p>    Cash flow			     45.4  vs  43.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Earlier this year NKF Holding NV took over Nokia</p>
<p>Cables Ltd, the cable division of NKF's previous majority</p>
<p>shareholder Nokia Oy.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
